From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:15:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: sticks, triggers, short presses and the mouse as
 a finger (#21)

The game got buttons only. Gamepad buttons arrived as one button because the C
side passed no button number, the sticks were never read, and a press shorter
than the time between two reads of the game was lost.

The input now reads the gamepad sticks (radial dead zone) and triggers (ZL and
ZR), can use the keyboard as sticks (NX2LINUX_KEYS_STICKS=1), keeps a button
that was released before the game read it until it has been read once and for
NX2LINUX_MIN_HOLD ms (50, 0 for the old behaviour, at most NX2LINUX_MAX_HOLD),
and gives the left mouse button as one finger on the touch screen with Start
and End. The end of the run prints what the game was given.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The game gets the gamepad sticks and triggers, short presses and a touch finger, which it did not before
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#21

